Campaigns — plan marketing activities and learn from them

PURPOSE
Newsletter, trade fair, ads: a small register of all marketing activities with period, budget
and what came out of it — so next year it is clear what was worth it.

DATA
One table "campaigns":
- title (text, required) — the activity, e.g. "Hanover fair 2026"
- channel (text) — e.g. email, fair, ads, social, print
- from_date (date) and to_date (date) — the period
- budget (number) — planned budget in euros
- spent (number) — actually spent
- leads (number) — contacts/inquiries gained
- status (text) — planned, running, done; new entries start as "planned"
- note (text) — learnings in keywords

Access: the whole team reads, marketing edits (scope "all").

VIEWS
A table overview "Campaigns" with activity, channel, period, budget, spent, leads and status.

TOOLS
The agent can create campaigns and update the numbers (consequential, with approval) and
query them (read-only) — e.g. "which campaign brought the most leads per euro?".
